  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through Tuesday)\nIssued at 1045 PM CDT Tue Aug 11 2026\n\nExtended range data from the latest suite of global models is in \ngeneral agreement that a subtropical high (centered from the Lower\nMS Valley to the southeastern Atlantic Coast) will continue to \nstrengthen this weekend, with geopotential heights perhaps \nreaching 600 dam. Thus, excessive heat will continue to be a \nconcern across the TN Valley, with highs remaining in the m-u 90s \nfrom Saturday-Monday (and perhaps exceeding 100F in several \nlocations on both Sunday and Monday afternoons). Although a few \nafternoon storms may occur on both Saturday and Sunday (primarily \nin the higher terrain of northeast AL), rain chances will remain \nlow and there is a very high chance that the pre-existing Heat \nAdvisory will need to be extended through Monday, perhaps with an \nupgrade to an Extreme Heat Warning due to Heat Index readings \nsurpassing 110F. By late in the forecast period, there are \nindications that the subtropical high may begin to retrograde into\nthe southern High Plains, perhaps allowing NW flow aloft to \nbecome reestablished across our region by Monday/Tuesday. Should \nthis occur, a weak cold front may bring a broken line of showers \nand thunderstorms to the region Monday evening, followed by a \nslight drop in temperatures/dewpoints on Tuesday.",
